{
    "article_summary": "This article describes a metal-free photoredox-catalyzed intramolecular cyclization of N-aryl acrylamides to synthesize oxindole derivatives. The reaction utilizes 4CzIPN as an organic photocatalyst, visible light as the energy source, and is mediated by water and aliphatic aldehydes (like decanal) as additives. The method avoids strong acids and metal catalysts, providing high yields and broad substrate compatibility, including drug-like molecules.",
